11
00:58:20,869 --> 00:58:26,869
Downton Abbey is a 2019 historical drama film directed by Michael Engler from a screenplay by
Julian Fellowes, based on the television series of the same name created by Fellowes.

12
01:03:39,130 --> 01:03:45,130
The film continues the storyline from the series, with
much of the original cast returning.

13
01:08:57,391 --> 01:09:03,391
A sequel, Downton Abbey: A New Era, was released in the United Kingdom in April 2022 and a
second sequel, Downton Abbey: The Grand Finale, was released in September 2025.

14
01:14:15,652 --> 01:14:21,652
Set in 1927, this film depicts a royal visit to the
Crawley family's stately home in Yorkshire.

15
01:19:33,913 --> 01:19:39,913
As royal staff members descend on Downton, an assassin has
also arrived and attempts to kill the monarch.

16
01:24:52,173 --> 01:24:58,173
After the series ended, a film adaptation was reportedly being considered
in April 2016, with Fellowes working on an outline plot.

17
01:30:10,434 --> 01:30:16,434
The producers confirmed that a feature-length film would be made in July 2018, and principal photography started in London
later the following month, and in other places in England, including Shepperton Studios and Highclere Castle.

18
01:35:28,695 --> 01:35:34,695
Filming ended that November, with a $13–20 million budget.

19
01:40:46,956 --> 01:40:52,956
Downton Abbey premiered at the Odeon Luxe Leicester Square in London on 9 September 2019, and was released in
the United Kingdom on 13 September and in the United States on 20 September, by Focus Features.

20
01:46:05,217 --> 01:46:11,217
The film received generally positive reviews from
critics and grossed $194.7 million worldwide.

21
01:51:23,478 --> 01:51:29,478
The film explores themes of yorkshire, period drama,
upstairs downstairs, 1920s, based on tv series.

22
01:56:41,739 --> 01:56:47,739
The tone is emotional.
